SUMMARY:Candlelight Open House
DESCRIPTION:Experience Historic Ephrata Cloister in a whole new light – by candlelight! As the sun sets on Saturday\, November 14th\, the site’s pathways and buildings glow with the light of candles\, creating an unforgettable evening atmosphere throughout the grounds from 5:00pm-8:00pm. This self-guided event allows you to explore the illuminated grounds at your own pace. Step inside the historic buildings to encounter interpreters\, skilled craftspeople\, and historical demonstrators who will share the stories\, trades\, and traditions of Ephrata’s past. \nThroughout the night\, enjoy: \n\nFamily-friendly activities and happenings perfect for all ages.\nVendors and craftspeople displaying their unique\, handmade wares!\nPerformances by the Ephrata Cloister Chorus at 5:30pm and 6:30pm in the historic 1741 Meetinghouse. Seating is limited and available on a first-come\, first-served basis; wristbands are required for entry and are free with admission.\nFireside tales and tellings at the bonfire as well as sweet treats available by donation!\nCostumed interpreters in the cemetery to learn about Ephrata’s historic burial grounds.\nNight Hikes by the Creek to the Witness Tree at 5:15pm\, 6:15pm\, and 7:15pm\, hikes start at the Physician’s House! Groups are limited; spots are available on a first-come\, first-served basis.\nFood and drink will be available for purchase\, including delicious local donuts and hot beverages from WDonuts’ Dub Truck!\n\nDon’t miss this chance to experience the site’s rich history brought to life after dark.
URL:https://lancasterpa.com/events-calendar/candlelight-open-house/
LOCATION:Ephrata Cloister\, 632 West Main Street\, Ephrata\, PA\, 17522\, United States
CATEGORIES:Autumn,Children & Family Events,Christmas Events in Lancaster County,Christmas Tour,Community Interest,Ephrata, PA,Holiday,Museums,Outdoor Activities
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://lancasterpa.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Misc-Events-12.png
